{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change","id":120079,"title":"Sidereals and focus change","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-26T18:39:16-07:00","id":120079,"title":"Sidereals and focus change","content":"So I'm reading the original games of divinity and this is a passage I've read in several places.<br /> <br /> &quot;They made the sidereals, who were wise and mighty seers and weaver of spells but few in number and weaker in battle than the solar and lunar exalted&quot;<br /> <br /> So my question is when did weaver of spells change to martial artists? I mean the implication is that they were more traditional sorcerers compared to other exalts but none the less they were less about fighting and more about mystical might. When did that change and why use Martial arts instead of sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T18:47:24-07:00","id":120081,"title":"","content":"<i>Games of Divinity</i> was written somewhat simultaneously with <i>Exalted</i> I believe. Sidreals are noted as being the masters of the martial arts in their original description of the 1e corebook (which also in the first printing had the Endings anima as orange as a bonus). <i>Book of 3 Circles</i> and <i>Games of Divinity</i> seem to play up their ability to interact with spirits as tied with sorcery, and I think what ended up happening is alot of that became part of their inherent Charmset.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T19:19:56-07:00","id":120088,"title":"","content":"The Martial Arts were also written in a very... wonky manner. When Sidereal Martial Arts came out, Jenna Moran and the other writers for the line DID say they were inferior to how powerful you could get with native Charms of Solars and Lunars (you can find plenty of old, old writer quotes to that effect); they weren't meant to be the ultimate combat skill. Problem is, Jenna tuned them so damn high that it was basically impossible to write a stronger combat suite than them unless every charm read 'I win'.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Jenna herself could have written Solar and Lunar charms that could have beaten SMA, and could flow from the written Charms for both splats, but she is a goddamn genius. For everyone else, it just did not seem to flow, and Sidereals became the combat monsters, the absolute Exalted-killers of the setting, when that wasn't the intention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T19:44:07-07:00","id":120096,"title":"","content":"Yes but why make them combat abilities if they were supposed to be weaker anyway? Why not just keep them to something without that focus? If you are going to make them physically weak making a set of abilities that are focused on combat seems like a shitty thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T21:10:53-07:00","id":120129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120096#post120096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but why make them combat abilities if they were supposed to be weaker anyway? Why not just keep them to something without that focus? If you are going to make them physically weak making a set of abilities that are focused on combat seems like a shitty thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div> As far as I can tell, Solars get access to the highest level of everything that isn't unique to an exalt type. The unique Sidereal ability is Astrology and not Martial Arts. A Solar can learn and practice Sidereal Martial Arts but a native Solar Charm or Solar Circle Spell that does the same thing will be both easier for a Solar to learn and will be more flexible. Compare Magic-Shattering Strike and Adamant Countermagic with Spell Shattering Palm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2551-lucil","name":"Lucil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T21:19:20-07:00","id":120134,"title":"","content":"Well, my guess is that, Wuxia being one of the big inspirational building blocks of Exalted, they figured Sidereals (the &quot;wise Exalts&quot;) to be the best to hold the archetype of the mysterious old master who knows the ultimate styles","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T21:33:28-07:00","id":120144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120134#post120134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, my guess is that, Wuxia being one of the big inspirational building blocks of Exalted, they figured Sidereals (the &quot;wise Exalts&quot;) to be the best to hold the archetype of the mysterious old master who knows the ultimate styles</div> </div> </div> </div>This in a nutshell.<br /> <br /> Note again that early on, it was Sidereals who invented the Fivefold Dragon Styles and all that good stuff. They were the sifu Exalted in the original corebook, invented the styles that Terrestrials use to kill Solars, and also had some things to do with spirits and demons. The issue is as Colapso notes a bit. Sidereals weren't supposed to be the top dogs in combat, but the idea of SMA was somewhat fudnementally flawed as it worked with the usual Essence 6+ problem and fed into the idea of exponential Essence power growth.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T21:40:11-07:00","id":120148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120096#post120096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but why make them combat abilities if they were supposed to be weaker anyway? Why not just keep them to something without that focus? If you are going to make them physically weak making a set of abilities that are focused on combat seems like a shitty thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first of all, I would be cautious about taking any broad statements of &quot;weaker in battle&quot; too literally. It might be technically true after a fashion, but &quot;battle&quot; is a pretty broad term. Exalted is a heavily Wuxia-influenced game, which means the mechanical differences between splats include a lot of words devoted to &quot;what is their approach to fighting?&quot;; &quot;they are bad at it&quot; is not a very useful answer.<br /> <br /> However, Sidereals are supposed to have a sort of idiosyncratic approach to combat. A Lunar or Solar who chooses to specialize in combat is going to be straightforwardly good at beating people up and will generally do well in situations where you'd expect beating people up to be a useful solution.<br /> <br /> While Sidereals aren't <i>bad</i> at that (in that your SMA master is never going to be a slouch in a fight), their focus is more on esoteric, indirect powers, or monofocused high-risk high-reward strategies which require planning. They're heavily technical fighters, while Solars and Lunars tend to be more balanced. The perception of Sidereals as &quot;arcane&quot; ties into this -- attacking indirectly or using complex plans is a staple of that sort of character.<br /> <br /> It might help to realize that because of that, it's (generally) a mistake to compare Sidereals to Dawns. Sidereals don't usually fight like Dawns. I mean, they can, and they won't fall apart, but it's not their forte. Thematically Sidereals are a lot closer to Twilights. Every Sidereal, after all, is going to have arcane trickery of some sort up their sleeves, even if it's from their astrology or native charms or martial arts rather than sorcery; and they leverage that in order to win.<br /> <br /> So with that in mind, what does it mean for, say, Pattern Spider Touch to be an MA charm (whereas the Twilight is probably getting that kind of polymorph-other effect from Sorcery, if they want it?) What it means is that <i>for that sort of character</i> -- for an arcane-mystical-seer sort of archetype -- Sidereals are actually very good at combat, because their punching-people skill and their strange-mystical-enlightenment skill come from the same place; Sidereals (and ancient-martial-arts-sages in general) are about blending mystical enlightenment with the power to beat up an entire tavern full of people at once if they set you off.<br /> <br /> I suspect that the bit you quoted was written under the mindset of &quot;well they usually can't leap at a Dawn with no plan beyond murder and expect to win&quot;, which is technically true but misses the point.<br /> <br /> Also more importantly (most importantly) it's just a throwaway line in a book that was not about Sidereals, so it probably didn't have as much thought put into it as the stuff in the actual Sidereal books.<br /> <br /> Also also, belatedly: I just realized that in context, it's describing the <i>creation</i> of the Sidereals. That is to say, the idea was that Sidereals were not created for combat, but they said &quot;screw that, the Maidens are insane&quot; and invented SMA anyway. As I recall, 1e was clear on the fact that Sidereals invented SMA specifically in order to jailbreak their way past the not-intended-for-combat thesis the Maidens had built them with. So the actual answer to your question is that it changed, in-setting, when the Sidereals decided that they weren't happy with their limitations and found a way to break them by practicing MA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-27-2014, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T21:41:43-07:00","id":120149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120144#post120144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This in a nutshell.<br /> <br /> Note again that early on, it was Sidereals who invented the Fivefold Dragon Styles and all that good stuff. They were the sifu Exalted in the original corebook, invented the styles that Terrestrials use to kill Solars, and also had some things to do with spirits and demons. The issue is as Colapso notes a bit. Sidereals weren't supposed to be the top dogs in combat, but the idea of SMA was somewhat fudnementally flawed as it worked with the usual Essence 6+ problem and fed into the idea of exponential Essence power growth.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the question is to what extent that should stay in 3e. Since they have a chance to alter it again. Personally, I'm all for astrology being the best avenue for xp and power growth but that's just me. Clearly it'll take work but seeing how much effort is going into Exalted as a whole I really hope they don't brush over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T21:51:12-07:00","id":120155,"title":"","content":"Essence 6+ working exponentially and making stuff below it irrelevant is something we've been told is not the case anymore<br /> <br /> Sidereal Exalted have been since Day One the best at the martial arts and it fits them as the esoteric sage-teacher-sifu archeotype. SMA do exist in some form as I remember seeing bandied about and they'll probably remain the top dogs at those.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T21:52:42-07:00","id":120158,"title":"","content":"Also, making astrology the &quot;Best way to power and growth&quot; more or less makes it the One True Build. Which is stupid. Martial arts expertise, astrology, their own native Charms and I would presume sorcery will all add up to them being able to be intersting in a way that's not just pidgeon-holing them into their unique mechanic.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T21:56:58-07:00","id":120159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120158#post120158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, making astrology the &quot;Best way to power and growth&quot; more or less makes it the One True Build. Which is stupid. Martial arts expertise, astrology, their own native Charms and I would presume sorcery will all add up to them being able to be intersting in a way that's not just pidgeon-holing them into their unique mechanic.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it can never be sorcery seeing as how it peaks out. Martial arts pidgeon holes them more than astrology would so it would be better to make Astrology number one, MA second, and Sorcery an ever distant third. I think Astrology should be a bigger emphasis because it gives more character options. When it comes to focus in exalted unless something extremely major changes trying to work in everything at once isn't possible. Native charms still have the issue of being a closed charmset.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T22:01:46-07:00","id":120160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120159#post120159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it can never be sorcery seeing as how it peaks out. Martial arts pidgeon holes them more than astrology would so it would be better to make Astrology number one, MA second, and Sorcery an ever distant third. I think Astrology should be a bigger emphasis because it gives more character options. When it comes to focus in exalted unless something extremely major changes trying to work in everything at once isn't possible. Native charms still have the issue of being a closed charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fail how astrology, a mechanic not likely to be expanded after their book very much (maybe in Getimians) pidgeon-holes them more than MA or sorcery, things that will expand more or less continuously with new books and with Sidereals as their peerless MA vein are going to liekly have excuses to grab. Also with 3e making multiple style purchases less redundant.<br /> <br /> Astrology in the end is neat, but if you start putting more and more weight into Resplendencies, you might as well just expand the damend Charm set instead of offloading things into a funky subsystem for the sake of making it more interesting because reasons.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T22:03:15-07:00","id":120163,"title":"","content":"And all that aside, why even rank their skills and just say they're good at a lot of things, they have differing and diverse routes of power, and not worry about whether you push them being astrologers, sifus, mages, or ninjas too much?<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T22:11:32-07:00","id":120166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120163#post120163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all that aside, why even rank their skills and just say they're good at a lot of things, they have differing and diverse routes of power, and not worry about whether you push them being astrologers, sifus, mages, or ninjas too much?<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be the best possible solution, and I truly hope it happens.<br /> <br /> (To comment on the astrology thing, though, since I share it: I think people, myself included, feel like they don't want Sidereals to only be able to expand their competence in power in two of the twenty-five Abilities. Astrology at least nominally involves the whole range of Abilities, even if thus far it's been an anemic, overpriced, overcomplicated joke. It's true that we might as well just open the Sidereal Charmset, and that would be a better solution -- but the devs have said outright that they're not going to do that, so Astrology seems like the closest thing that might actually be vaguely viable.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T22:15:00-07:00","id":120168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120160#post120160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fail how astrology, a mechanic not likely to be expanded after their book very much (maybe in Getimians) pidgeon-holes them more than MA or sorcery, things that will expand more or less continuously with new books and with Sidereals as their peerless MA vein are going to liekly have excuses to grab. Also with 3e making multiple style purchases less redundant.<br /> <br /> Astrology in the end is neat, but if you start putting more and more weight into Resplendencies, you might as well just expand the damend Charm set instead of offloading things into a funky subsystem for the sake of making it more interesting because reasons.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer Astrology to be a set of rituals/spells that are potent but ultimately allow for a kind of advancement that gives them power while resticting their charm capabilities. If Astrology doesn't get expanded on then that would be like Knacks not getting expanded on at this point or elemental magic being removed from the dragon-blooded. Everyone seems to conveniently ignore that they aren't the SIFU exalted. They aren't the Martial arts exalted. They are sidereals, they are the Hands of Fate. The are the Astrological exalted. You can't just brush astrology aside without removing the very core power they are supposed to have access to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120160#post120160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all that aside, why even rank their skills and just say they're good at a lot of things, they have differing and diverse routes of power, and not worry about whether you push them being astrologers, sifus, mages, or ninjas too much?<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because these are the things that sidereals have been pushed to for growth. The only problem is Astrology never lived up to the expectations, sorcery was always something they were in second place with, and sifus were something they all had to be if they wanted to stay relevant in combat past 500xp. They have a limited charmset so they have limited options when it comes to growth. I don't think it's an issue but I think which should stay as the best avenue should change from martial artists to astrologers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T22:27:22-07:00","id":120170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120168#post120168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd prefer Astrology to be a set of rituals/spells that are potent but ultimately allow for a kind of advancement that gives them power while resticting their charm capabilities. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically another pseudo-sorcery system?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120168#post120168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... If Astrology doesn't get expanded on then that would be like Knacks not getting expanded on at this point or elemental magic being removed from the dragon-blooded. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Knacks are going away in 3e, and elemental magic is done just fine with native DB Charms instead of making a subsystem for bending. So I still fail to see how things are any less pidgeon-holed besides some ambiguous idealized thing in your head saying it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120168#post120168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Everyone seems to conveniently ignore that they aren't the SIFU exalted. They aren't the Martial arts exalted. They are sidereals, they are the Hands of Fate. The are the Astrological exalted. You can't just brush astrology aside without removing the very core power they are supposed to have access to.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are peerless martial artists. They are oracles. They are the Obi Wan, the Kheshmet, the Pai Mei. Fate at their core means nothing without a strong genre and thematic to them to draw on. And part of that is the image of the wisend master is being a guy who trains heroes and knows kung fu. Fate is the core of their power, but martial arts have always been a part of the manfiestation of that power and that thematic.<br /> <br /> I again also don't see why if you are going to give them a bunch of single-buy magic powers in cascades, might as well just roll those into the Charms they have and flesh out the underloved Abilities ala the new Solar Charmset so you can just spend lots of xp in one, still seem awesome and nto seem like you are ever going to run-out of options unless you go into subsystems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120168#post120168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because these are the things that sidereals have been pushed to for growth. The only problem is Astrology never lived up to the expectations, sorcery was always something they were in second place with, and sifus were something they all had to be if they wanted to stay relevant in combat past 500xp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly what, might I ask, were the expectations for Astrology other than special hoodoo? Necromancy and shapeshifting made the range so wide that I had really no expectations going in and thought Resplendencies were more or less a set of extra powers with a bullshit clunky subsystem to get to. And see my post above. If you have more Charms to actually expand into, you don't run out of htings to expand into later on. Making sorcery more relevant at the Celestial Circle might be nice too, unless your philsophy here is Adamant magics or go home I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120168#post120168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have a limited charmset so they have limited options when it comes to growth. I don't think it's an issue but I think which should stay as the best avenue should change from martial artists to astrologers</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why one has to exclude the other, or why this is even a dichotomy to worry about.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T22:31:29-07:00","id":120171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change#post120079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm reading the original games of divinity and this is a passage I've read in several places.<br /> <br /> &quot;They made the sidereals, who were wise and mighty seers and weaver of spells but few in number and weaker in battle than the solar and lunar exalted&quot;<br /> <br /> So my question is when did weaver of spells change to martial artists? I mean the implication is that they were more traditional sorcerers compared to other exalts but none the less they were less about fighting and more about mystical might. When did that change and why use Martial arts instead of sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem comes from the fact that when Exalted 1st Edition was first being written up, it was directly linked to what is now oWoD. In fact the original promotional material for it used the concept that the prehistory of the world as we know it is a lie.<br /> <br /> Each Exalt type was supposed to be the super powered ancestor of each of the core splats of the world of darkness setting. In fact if you look closer at the old books, you can see hold over mechanics from each splat.<br /> <br /> Abyssal = Cainite Vampire<br /> Dragon-Blooded = Kuei-Jin Vampire<br /> Lunar = Werewolf<br /> Solar = Hunter<br /> <br /> And last but not least was the Sidereals as the Mage analog. Why Martial Arts if they were supposed to be the grand magic users of the Exalted setting you ask, because back then the concept of &quot;Do&quot; the magic based martial art of the Akashic Brotherhood was still a central concept.<br /> <br /> So yeah, that's the entire reason Sidereals are the way they are, aside from constantly being written up in such a way that they only make sense as NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T22:37:52-07:00","id":120173,"title":"","content":"I think that -- while Astrology should be cool and useful and a viable place to devote your character -- overall, complaining that your Sidereal has to be a wise martial arts sifu in order to advance gets into &quot;stupid dog, why aren't you a cat&quot; territory. Martial Arts are meant to be utterly central to the Sidereal experience and to Sidereal thematics; I think that turning it into &quot;just something some Sidereals happen to do&quot; would lose a lot of what makes them what they are.<br /> <br /> (The lotus analogies are not just for show. Sidereals are meant to <i>change</i> as they increase in power -- that's part of what their closed charm trees are about. If you play a Lunar or a Solar -- I mean, at E2, you do something, and at E5, you do the same thing, but much bigger or grander or more overwhelmingly. That's not meant to be how Sidereals work, I think, and that distinction was a deliberate choice.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T22:42:58-07:00","id":120176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120170#post120170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are peerless martial artists. They are oracles. They are the Obi Wan, the Kheshmet, the Pai Mei. Fate at their core means nothing without a strong genre and thematic to them to draw on. And part of that is the image of the wisend master is being a guy who trains heroes and knows kung fu. Fate is the core of their power, but martial arts have always been a part of the manfiestation of that power and that thematic.<br /> <br /> I again also don't see why if you are going to give them a bunch of single-buy magic powers in cascades, might as well just roll those into the Charms they have and flesh out the underloved Abilities ala the new Solar Charmset so you can just spend lots of xp in one, still seem awesome and nto seem like you are ever going to run-out of options unless you go into subsystems.<br /> <br /> <br /> Exactly what, might I ask, were the expectations for Astrology other than special hoodoo? Necromancy and shapeshifting made the range so wide that I had really no expectations going in and thought Resplendencies were more or less a set of extra powers with a bullshit clunky subsystem to get to. And see my post above. If you have more Charms to actually expand into, you don't run out of htings to expand into later on. Making sorcery more relevant at the Celestial Circle might be nice too, unless your philsophy here is Adamant magics or go home I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't see why one has to exclude the other, or why this is even a dichotomy to worry about.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kungfu is nice but it forces every sidereal to be a kungfu master. They can never be peerless sorcerers (or peerless martial arts if we are talking about it from a king of the hill perspective) because that belongs to the Solars (and specific exigents if you decide to use them). Astrology is literally a way to control fate. Martial arts and being sifus is a passive and rather narrow role that has being LAUDED as the best and only way to go right now. If something has to be in this position. It should be astrology. It shouldn't be Martial arts. Martial arts is definitely something they should be good at, but they have always been about manipulating fate and being peerless oracles over everything else. <br /> <br /> It's not about excluding the other it's about one thing being better than everything else and for sidereals this is martial arts in 1e and 2e. I wouldn't mind Astrology and MA being equal but if one has to be BETTER. Then I don't want it to be MA for a third time in a row. I want it to be Astrology. I WANT to use astrology and FEEL good about using it while having access to a unique ability only Sidereals have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T22:47:54-07:00","id":120177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120173#post120173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that -- while Astrology should be cool and useful and a viable place to devote your character -- overall, complaining that your Sidereal has to be a wise martial arts sifu in order to advance gets into &quot;stupid dog, why aren't you a cat&quot; territory. Martial Arts are meant to be utterly central to the Sidereal experience and to Sidereal thematics; I think that turning it into &quot;just something some Sidereals happen to do&quot; would lose a lot of what makes them what they are.<br /> <br /> (The lotus analogies are not just for show. Sidereals are meant to <i>change</i> as they increase in power -- that's part of what their closed charm trees are about. If you play a Lunar or a Solar -- I mean, at E2, you do something, and at E5, you do the same thing, but much bigger or grander or more overwhelmingly. That's not meant to be how Sidereals work, I think, and that distinction was a deliberate choice.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals have large portions text devoted to astrology despite it being really bad and really useless. It's possible to keep Martial arts and lotus analogies while making astrology the strongest tool in their kit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T22:58:02-07:00","id":120190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120176#post120176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kungfu is nice but it forces every sidereal to be a kungfu master. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? I just stated ways to avoid it without getting rid of it. Focus on your native Charmset. Make said set bigger. Done. It should also be noted that in 3e since MA isn't necessarily tied to the MA Ability, you have more ways to branch in that anyhow. Sidereals being best at kung fu makes them all kung fu masters in teh same way Solars being best at Evocations and sorcery maek them all the best weaponmasters or sorcerers. It's an option, not the only route.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120176#post120176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... They can never be peerless sorcerers (or peerless martial arts if we are talking about it from a king of the hill perspective) because that belongs to the Solars (and specific exigents if you decide to use them). ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when does an option have to be the best to be an option? Sidereals likely have spells that are lost to most other Exalts. And as a note, unless I missed something, Sidereals always paid less xp for SMA, spent less motes (sutras) and could make new ones. In 3e, while no more Essence 6+ stuff is about, I don't see where Solars are expected to be the best MAists when Sidereal Martial Arts is sitll a thing. And what themes the Exigent has to make them compete is irrelevant, as that could be said with any Exalt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120176#post120176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Astrology is literally a way to control fate. Martial arts and being sifus is a passive and rather narrow role that has being LAUDED as the best and only way to go right now. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate in Creation is causality. There's already a shitload of magic that does that, and besides dice manipulation, it's mostly a grab bag of effects. Expanding it simply does that further. It has some neat effects, mind. But in the end, expanding astrology makes it special-secret sorcery as both are reality warping based on what Exalted has billed fate as. And even with the martial arts emphasis, it has been <i>among</i> their strengths. You complain about one pidgeon hole and then toss things in antoher. It's textbook false dichotomy at work here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120176#post120176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... If something has to be in this position. It should be astrology. It shouldn't be Martial arts. Martial arts is definitely something they should be good at, but they have always been about manipulating fate and being peerless oracles over everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does that have to be a super special subsystem and not be powerful Charms they're competent in? You know, like Lunars beyond the basic shapeshifting power are in 1e and 3e? Or how Terrestrials are with elemental magic without some special bending subsystem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120176#post120176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about excluding the other it's about one thing being better than everything else and for sidereals this is martial arts in 1e and 2e. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Their Charmset also had some of the best battlefield buffs, inherent spirit-relation magic, weird shit, and some of the best defensive tech about. They were de facto best at astrology since well, no one else could even use it. So I fail to see the issue here unless the complaint is they didn't get more wordcount ot a subsystem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120176#post120176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I wouldn't mind Astrology and MA being equal but if one has to be BETTER. Then I don't want it to be MA for a third time in a row. I want it to be Astrology. I WANT to use astrology and FEEL good about using it while having access to a unique ability only Sidereals have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the issue I have with this entire argument is you have no postive thesis. All you are saying is that you want something different becuase it's not what's been before. It's the belief that anything not the status quo is inherently superior, while not actually questioning what your position actually is. What the hell would this supposed primary fate magic be that isn't a layer of pseudo-Charms/spells that could of just as easily been effects in the native Charmset already capable of fate-bending? And why does anything have or should be assumed as prioritized, toher than worked to a whole?<br /> <br /> What exactly is a fatebender? What exactly do you want a Sidereal to be? What genre, or sort of characters do you get? I ask this since so far all you've said is you think a fate focus is better, but Sidreals <i>already</i> are fate and symbolism focused. It just so happens is that the characters that draw on that <i>also draw on Martial Arts master themes</i> and the game is one with a kung fu system. It fits Sidereals and is part of Sidereals as well. And what to do to expand things is unclear on your part other than statements that &quot;It is because I think it is&quot; so far.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T23:13:08-07:00","id":120199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120190#post120190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? I just stated ways to avoid it without getting rid of it. Focus on your native Charmset. Make said set bigger. Done. It should also be noted that in 3e since MA isn't necessarily tied to the MA Ability, you have more ways to branch in that anyhow. Sidereals being best at kung fu makes them all kung fu masters in teh same way Solars being best at Evocations and sorcery maek them all the best weaponmasters or sorcerers. It's an option, not the only route.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can never make the charmset too big or you open the charmset up. Which is never going to happen. You need an area for growth. Kung fu has been the only option. The only option. I'm not saying to nerf MA I'm saying to make Astrology stronger without making it boring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120190#post120190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since when does an option have to be the best to be an option? Sidereals likely have spells that are lost to most other Exalts. And as a note, unless I missed something, Sidereals always paid less xp for SMA, spent less motes (sutras) and could make new ones. In 3e, while no more Essence 6+ stuff is about, I don't see where Solars are expected to be the best MAists when Sidereal Martial Arts is sitll a thing. And what themes the Exigent has to make them compete is irrelevant, as that could be said with any Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals can never get Adamant sorcery. They are stuck with Sapphire sorcery. They can't even get the second circle of necromancy. As for SMA, it's definitely nice. Solar Hero style is still stronger than it on every level. From a pure combat perspective, doesn't matter how many martial arts you have when a solar can just beat you down other than enlightenment which again means nothing when you get beaten down. With Gementian's having full access to SMA this just makes the best martial artist mean even less in the face of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120190#post120190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate in Creation is causality. There's already a shitload of magic that does that, and besides dice manipulation, it's mostly a grab bag of effects. Expanding it simply does that further. It has some neat effects, mind. But in the end, expanding astrology makes it special-secret sorcery as both are reality warping based on what Exalted has billed fate as. And even with the martial arts emphasis, it has been <i>among</i> their strengths. You complain about one pidgeon hole and then toss things in antoher. It's textbook false dichotomy at work here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Astrology is a much wider tool and has more applicability. SMA forces every sidereal have MA 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120190#post120190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does that have to be a super special subsystem and not be powerful Charms they're competent in? You know, like Lunars beyond the basic shapeshifting power are in 1e and 3e? Or how Terrestrials are with elemental magic without some special bending subsystem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Astrology was a subsystem just done poorly. If it's in their native charms only well they'll hit a wall just like everything within the CLOSED charmset that they have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120190#post120190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their Charmset also had some of the best battlefield buffs, inherent spirit-relation magic, weird shit, and some of the best defensive tech about. They were de facto best at astrology since well, no one else could even use it. So I fail to see the issue here unless the complaint is they didn't get more wordcount ot a subsystem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you pretending astrology was good? WHY are you even remotely defending astrology when it has been the worst system in the game for two years running. It's a poor system that needs to be improved. And has always meant be a usable system. It was just done by people who didn't know how to do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120190#post120190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the issue I have with this entire argument is you have no postive thesis. All you are saying is that you want something different becuase it's not what's been before. It's the belief that anything not the status quo is inherently superior, while not actually questioning what your position actually is. What the hell would this supposed primary fate magic be that isn't a layer of pseudo-Charms/spells that could of just as easily been effects in the native Charmset already capable of fate-bending? And why does<br /> anything have or should be assumed as prioritized, toher than worked to a whole?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because again astrology, Martial arts and sorcery have always been the three purported avenues of expansion and astrology plain sucks, sorcery hits a wall as a non-solar, and Martial arts has literally been the thing every sidereal is supposed go into or they will never gain any power. Do you think this is good do you think this is how it should be? Because if you do we won't agree. Chejak in his current writeup has about 1k experience in astrology and it's fucking useless. Do you think that's good? I don't for a man who has colleges at SEVEN. IT should mean something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120190#post120190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is a fatebender? What exactly do you want a Sidereal to be? What genre, or sort of characters do you get? I ask this since so far all you've said is you think a fate focus is better, but Sidreals <i>already</i> are fate and symbolism focused. It just so happens is that the characters that draw on that <i>also draw on Martial Arts master themes</i> and the game is one with a kung fu system. It fits Sidereals and is part of Sidereals as well. And what to do to expand things is unclear on your part other than statements that &quot;It is because I think it is&quot; so far.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>HOnestly, I'm not sure yet. I just want astrology to have a purpose one that doesn't involve being a way to break the game or a shitty disguise system that's trumped by one charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-27-2014, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T23:37:10-07:00","id":120209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120176#post120176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Kungfu is nice but it forces every sidereal to be a kungfu master.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm currently playing a Sidereal of Venus who does not practice Martial Arts. Her combat Charms consist of the 2nd Melee Excellency, Defense of Shining Joy, and the Performance Excellencies. She has 453XP and has yet to be injured in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2551-lucil","name":"Lucil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T23:40:34-07:00","id":120211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120199#post120199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can never make the charmset too big or you open the charmset up. Which is never going to happen. You need an area for growth. Kung fu has been the only option. The only option. I'm not saying to nerf MA I'm saying to make Astrology stronger without making it boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>As-is, it's impossible to buy all the Charms in the set without spending in excees of one-thousand xp. Simply making trees that are only four or five Charms long a bit longer is not going to end the world on closed Charmset options and pushes that number higher. <br /> <br /> Again, I have yet to be told how astrology being stronger ins't just a bunch of pseudo-Charms, since a lot of Sidereal Charms as-is look like spells with Charm timing, and the Greater Astrology in late 2e was not much different either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120199#post120199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals can never get Adamant sorcery. They are stuck with Sapphire sorcery. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh perish the thought you're stuck at being one of a few hundred people in the world to use Sapphire magics. Might as well not bother if you aren't allowed Adamant. What a waste of time if you can't get to the top.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120199#post120199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.. They can't even get the second circle of necromancy. ...</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not like necromancy mechanically had a point. And we don't know the structure of either in 3e to go and make claims of how much a Sidereal is limitted or at a loss for &quot;only&quot; getting the second Circle of Sorcery. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120199#post120199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... As for SMA, it's definitely nice. Solar Hero style is still stronger than it on every level. From a pure combat perspective, doesn't matter how many martial arts you have when a solar can just beat you down other than enlightenment which again means nothing when you get beaten down. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because building your argument on what 3e should be by arguing from a place where 2e is acknoweldged to not fucking work helps. 2e power is moot here. Sidereals are the best MAs of the traditional Exalted. They probably remain this in 3e. And since the game seems to run less on raw huge numbers and one-shots, that might make that esoteric weirdness of SMA more interesting to actually put to use and feel neat and esoteric and symbolic and shit. You know, stuff other than generic &quot;Fate bendy dude who does fate stuff because fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120199#post120199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... With Gementian's having full access to SMA this just makes the best martial artist mean even less in the face of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wudon v. Shaolin is less an intersting fight when there's not enemy kung fu guys. Them being peers is there because of thematics. Going about saying Exalt sorts are defined soley in how much better than everyone else because is missing hte point on some fo the things. Solars get the best Evocations and sorcery becuase in part thematics (heroes like Solars tend to be the sort to go for forbidden knowledge or powerful weapons). Sidereals being best at kung fu is because they're again, the the ones going around being the oracles, guides and Obi Wans. Getimians get it because their hero type is Daoist alchemists and evil onmyoujis, and it works on their internal magics. An Exalt type is more than just &quot;I'm best at this.&quot; You already have a unique Charmset no one else gets and a limitted club mebmership to SMA and astrology that does some esoteric stuff already. I fail to see in the end how someone getting to eat from the cookie jar somehow devalues a grou's worth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120199#post120199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astrology is a much wider tool and has more applicability. SMA forces every sidereal have MA 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>3e Archery, Melee and Thrown have styles too. Otehr Abilities may as well. And well, you might just focus on native Charms. War is pretty big, so is Larceny, Stealth, Lore and Investigation. You could just be a loremaster. That's nearly a hundred xp to get there.<br /> <br /> This is also premised a bit on you know, astrology actually being broader. You have yet to say what it is other than again, broader because you say it is and obviously not kung fu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120199#post120199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astrology was a subsystem just done poorly. If it's in their native charms only well they'll hit a wall just like everything within the CLOSED charmset that they have.</div> </div> </div> </div>So how many 250+ session games have you played? Or do you just get bored with Sidereal Charms themselves and move on? I mean, a lot of Solars seem to go along well in their lives never touching a homebrew Charm, spell or MA Charm. 3e is being built to make that easier. Why can't Sidereals just have more options in the native set to be interesting? I mean, SIdereals are always going to have the best Sidereal Charms and those tend to be neat as hell on their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120199#post120199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you pretending astrology was good? WHY are you even remotely defending astrology when it has been the worst system in the game for two years running. It's a poor system that needs to be improved. And has always meant be a usable system. It was just done by people who didn't know how to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue shaping combat is worst, personally. It was also, as a historical note, done by GCG originally (who liked the system for its representaitonal aspects and because he didnt' wnat it to be another pseudo-sorcery) and StephenLS (who made it clear, just kind of didn't fix the Byzantine part of it). The Dreams version is alright. <br /> <br /> Still, what's the alternative? Not this? Okay, what's not this? What's you're positive thesis? Astrology is bad, not doubting that. I am not sure what the hell you want it to be that's not covered by Charms or sucha thing that doesn't just make it another necromancy or weaving: neat pseudo-sorcery that gets abandoned because other shit needs to be talked about over time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120199#post120199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because again astrology, Martial arts and sorcery have always been the three purported avenues of expansion and astrology plain sucks, sorcery hits a wall as a non-solar, and Martial arts has literally been the thing every sidereal is supposed go into or they will never gain any power.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you hit a wall that includes Demon of the Second Circle and there's litereally about sixty people in the world with the ability and give-a-shit to get the higher Circle, and since you can buy infintie spells at that level...I fail to see how it's really a wall I guess. Again, if you can't go Adamant don't come play at all is your statement here?<br /> <br /> And unless you magically get every single Charm published (doubtful), you probably have enough room to expand for a while in being just a cool Sidereal that I fail to see the issue. Especially since as I gather a lot of the weird ritual fate magic shit you want a subsystem so much for is in the native Charm as is and probably can be done as just more native Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120199#post120199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think this is good do you think this is how it should be? Because if you do we won't agree. Chejak in his current writeup has about 1k experience in astrology and it's fucking useless. Do you think that's good? I don't for a man who has colleges at SEVEN. IT should mean something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Colleges are shit. I'm not arguing that. I also don't think the solution is another psuedo-sorcery just &quot;Fate themed&quot;, which is, as I can gather, bitchign at spiders and using symbology instead of just reweaving reality at the post-coding phase.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120199#post120199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HOnestly, I'm not sure yet. I just want astrology to have a purpose one that doesn't involve being a way to break the game or a shitty disguise system that's trumped by one charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't necessitate it be some thing that &quot;if I have to make one or the other the priority of Sidereals it should be it.&quot; Honestly, I feel over time astrology is a bit forced when other splats in the end did magic effects just fine withotu it having to be a third wheel system like sorcery.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T23:51:16-07:00","id":120218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120211#post120211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 3e Archery, Melee and Thrown have styles too. Otehr Abilities may as well. And well, you might just focus on native Charms. War is pretty big, so is Larceny, Stealth, Lore and Investigation. You could just be a loremaster. That's nearly a hundred xp to get there.<br /> <br /> This is also premised a bit on you know, astrology actually being broader. You have yet to say what it is other than again, broader because you say it is and obviously not kung fu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since we aren't agreeing and this'll just get longer and longer. I just want to address this. Yeah other combat styles are going to go into other combat abilities but honestly, if they hit other abilities in general it'll be very against what martial arts has been. Yes you can focus on native charms but after a long run or maybe if you want something else outside of sidereal charms for abilities you might not be able to get. Astrology should be about planning the future altering causality in some minor or grand way. Being able to use the stars for a host of effects. It should be grand but subtle and yeah it shouldn't be like MA in any way. However, if we have to shove sidereals into one hole after the sidereal native charms I would want it to be astrology over martial arts. That said I would prefer them both be equal powerwise at the very least. I also feel it should remain a subsystem because their native charmset while being very fate driven isn't astrological in any direct way and for the most part, sidereal charms except one or two aren't Spell-like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T05:15:34-07:00","id":120293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120173#post120173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">overall, complaining that your Sidereal has to be a wise martial arts sifu in order to advance gets into &quot;stupid dog, why aren't you a cat&quot; territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can look at it that way, I guess? At a certain level it comes down to taste and breadth of options. I dig wise martial arts sifu Sidereals, and the idea that all Sidereals end up being that way after long enough is just so <i>boring</i>. At a certain level, I think &quot;clear and evocative thesis&quot; should be secondary to &quot;fun to play, both the first time and over and over.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T08:36:20-07:00","id":120353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120211#post120211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh perish the thought you're stuck at being one of a few hundred people in the world to use Sapphire magics. Might as well not bother if you aren't allowed Adamant. What a waste of time if you can't get to the top.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least Raksi agrees with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T09:24:53-07:00","id":120378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120353#post120353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least Raksi agrees with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would note that isn't a point in his favor. It's like the argument of &quot;It worked in Voyager's depiction of X&quot; for me.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T09:31:50-07:00","id":120382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120378#post120378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would note that isn't a point in his favor. It's like the argument of &quot;It worked in Voyager's depiction of X&quot; for me.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was the joke. Though it can be tricky to tell one or the other over the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T09:35:18-07:00","id":120384,"title":"","content":"Agree on breadth and character being important. When we have these threads, I do think part of the problem is that people talk about Sidereals in a way that homogenises them.<br /> <br /> With Solars, we'd be talking about how there should be clear and differentiated paths for Castes, and within that, for different characters within a Caste.<br /> <br /> Whereas with Sidereals and Lunars it feels a lot more like so long as there is a Sidereal or Lunar path, then there isn't much sensitivity to context for character or caste.<br /> <br /> Take an example of a Sidereal Caste, the Journeys, just because they're the first in the book - <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;In the First Age, the Chosen of Journeys were charged with maintaining and expanding the complex web of transportation and communication networks that spanned all of Creation. Under their management, every kind of commodity moved quickly and efficiently from one corner of the world to another... the Chosen of Journeys saw to it that this vast web was turned against the world's fallen rulers ... and the Dragon-Blooded out manuevered their former lords at every step.&quot;</i> and goes on from there.<br /> <br /> So this stuff is pretty cool right? And increasingly powerful diverse and character sensitive expressions of this kind of theme, the theme of Journeys, should be what a Sidereals of the Journeys Caste should be able to draw on as he becomes stronger, more than him becoming a *generic* powerful Sidereal with a lot of powers that are interchangeable between different Castes and character concepts.<br /> <br /> From this kind of perspective, I can see why magic based on Astrological Colleges might be more appealing than Martial Arts. Martial Arts could make a character into a sort of generic peerless sifu, and seems less naturally to enhance a character as a character and as a character of a particular Caste, with a given role in changing the world in specific ways.<br /> <br /> (Also, isn't Raksi doing the opposite of giving up learning Celestial Sorcery because she can't get Adamant, in the sense of learning it thoroughly while also trying to overcome her limits (in a sort of mad, baby eating sort of way)?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T10:45:57-07:00","id":120404,"title":"","content":"You know... what about making Astrology something like meta-Evocations for the 25 constellations? First, you have to learn the fundamentals of the college (the Ability). Then, you can train in the mystic arts of the college (the Charm). Then you can train in something like the destiny of the college, or the nature of the college (Astrology). This could fit in with Sidereal themes a number of ways.<br /> <br /> 1) Evocations that change the nature of a skill in some way. Solars are still the best at using the skill. But Sidereals understand the nature of the skill better, so they can apply it in round-about ways. A solar can hit you with a table, or a sword. He can even swing the table like a sword, and might just rip you in half, but he's never going to slit your jugular with that table. The Sidereal could pick up the table, and say, &quot;Through my understanding of the College of Melee, this table is a melee weapon, like a rapier, and so can do rapier-like things,&quot; and perfectly pierce you through the heart with it.<br /> <br /> 2) Evocations that alter the nature of a charm in some way. Maybe even let Sidereals research or discover 'new' evocations in a College. The constellations are huge, amazingly powerful things, and it would probably be silly to say Sidereals know everything that can be done with them. Lock off Greater Astrology as before, but give them a nice run of possible evocations written up, and let them research how to use their Abilities and Charms a bit more flexibility. I'm thinking something like 'Take an Charm from another ability, apply it to the use of this skill, in this situation.' For example, let's take a theoretical Endurance charm that lets you go without food. You know that charm, and you know an evocation in the College of Medicine that modifies it in a particular way. Something like: &quot;While you have this Evocation active, you cannot use the Endurance charm in its normal manner. You can, however, apply it to one other creature as a Medicine charm.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) Let the Sidereals keep giving an astrological blessing, but simply the rules. Make the benefit something resembling a specialty dot, make it easier to give, restrict the number of dots he can hand out, make it for a fixed duration, a hero can only have one astrological blessing at a time, and the effect can be changed until it runs out, but it can be renewed. Something like 'You three heroes get a one-dot specialty in Melee when fighting side-by-side-by-side, for a period of one week.'<br /> <br /> This would allow Sidereals to actually work destiny to some extent: If someone has a Geas that they will only be killed by a rapier, the Sidereal can rework the situation to take advantage of it, even if he doesn't have a rapier. This would also give Sidereals more flexibility in their current charm set by applying them in other places. Honestly, the Sidereal charmset already does this to a great extent. If a Sidereal wants to steal his opponents armor, he uses Larceny. However, Soak is kind of like armor, so the Sidereal says close enough, and steals some Soak. Or, if a Sidereal wants to steal his opponent's knowledge, he can steal his journals. However, thoughts are kind of like a journal, so the Sidereal steals that instead. Finally, this would let the wise sage say 'The prophecy supports this,' or the wise Sifu who teaches the three heroes one particular fancy technique, and it has immediate applicability.<br /> <br /> Do some cost-balancing things (Dots in a college, or just access to the college, plus evocations from the college?) some fine-tuning, and voila, you have a flexible, useful, and in-theme astrology that doesn't require its own subsystem (except in a very small way for #3).<br /> <br /> This idea is VERY unrefined, but I think it is sufficiently simple and elegant enough to fit into whatever Sidereals end up doing in 3rd, and sufficiently easy to houserule into effect for 2.5 games. Doesn't look unbalanced on the surface to me (probably because there are no actual rules there yet). And I think this is very in theme with how Sidereals would do things.<br /> <br /> Last thought... An evocation for Alchemy that would let you turn what would normally be a potion of strength for a human into a potion of super-bouncing for bears. (80s/90s cartoon reference, for those who haven't seen the cartoon in question).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T12:23:50-07:00","id":120457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120218#post120218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since we aren't agreeing and this'll just get longer and longer. I just want to address this. Yeah other combat styles are going to go into other combat abilities but honestly, if they hit other abilities in general it'll be very against what martial arts has been. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how. MA has been a grab bag combat Ability that stepped on the toes of other Abilities. That was part of the Sidereal issue, in that when you finished their short Melee or Brawl tree, you had MA or bust. Having styles for the other Abilties helps in the area that people spend a lot of xp on anyhow: Combat Charms. And it makes it so that if you want to be a guy using swords, you can stick to Melee isntead of dipping into MA constantly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120218#post120218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Yes you can focus on native charms but after a long run or maybe if you want something else outside of sidereal charms for abilities you might not be able to get. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is any Exalt sort. Most people don't homebrew Charms, and you go for non-native stuff when you want to break out of your conceptual space. Solars do this easily since &quot;paragon of skill&quot; is kind of shallow conceptual space. Symbolic Weird Shit and viceral body-crafting are a bit less so. Sidereals should be appealing because in part they don't need to break out to get esoteric weird stuff. It's not like an open set gives Solars and other Exalts carte blanche ability to go and just be whatever they want, less so in 3e with things like Charmshare being tossed out for the most part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120218#post120218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Astrology should be about planning the future altering causality in some minor or grand way. Being able to use the stars for a host of effects. It should be grand but subtle and yeah it shouldn't be like MA in any way. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have yet to see an example of this not already done with the Greater Astrology or inherent Sidereal magic can't achieve though. And the former were in the end strong Charms with College prerequisites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120218#post120218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... However, if we have to shove sidereals into one hole after the sidereal native charms I would want it to be astrology over martial arts. That said I would prefer them both be equal powerwise at the very least. I also feel it should remain a subsystem because their native charmset while being very fate driven isn't astrological in any direct way and for the most part, sidereal charms except one or two aren't Spell-like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of the Lore tree does prediction and dictating Fate. You can create coincidences and have esoteric rituals with their prayer strip stuff. You can make a heavenly-bound decree to defeat spirits and turn them into Artifacts. <br /> <br /> Fate magic to me in the end is a lot of consequences and controlling that on the basis of the symbology of the constellations and the plaents. Which native Charms and Greater Astrology do fine now. Unless you are going to take time to show how it's so special from either native Charms or sorcery, it's moot.<br /> <br /> Again, all I see is a want for a subsystem to have some ambiguous Fate magic that you have given me limts and fancy words as to what it is, but I have yet to be told what it should be able to do in a concrete way besides, &quot;Not be MA or native Charms.&quot;<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T12:35:01-07:00","id":120462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120404#post120404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last thought... An evocation for Alchemy that would let you turn what would normally be a potion of strength for a human into a potion of super-bouncing for bears. (80s/90s cartoon reference, for those who haven't seen the cartoon in question).</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cmQbNusgGNI\" target=\"_blank\">Even better, it's not classified as a drug by the DEA!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T12:46:04-07:00","id":120469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120457#post120457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of the Lore tree does prediction and dictating Fate. You can create coincidences and have esoteric rituals with their prayer strip stuff. You can make a heavenly-bound decree to defeat spirits and turn them into Artifacts.<br /> <br /> Fate magic to me in the end is a lot of consequences and controlling that on the basis of the symbology of the constellations and the plaents. Which native Charms and Greater Astrology do fine now. Unless you are going to take time to show how it's so special from either native Charms or sorcery, it's moot.<br /> <br /> Again, all I see is a want for a subsystem to have some ambiguous Fate magic that you have given me limts and fancy words as to what it is, but I have yet to be told what it should be able to do in a concrete way besides, &quot;Not be MA or native Charms.&quot;<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Martial arts steps on toes very lightly and it's all focused on combat. No matter the charm. Martial arts are still combat charms focused around combat revolving around combat in some shape or form.<br /> <br /> I'd have a system if I knew how sidereals were going to work and if I had the time to create one. There are so many ways to go about it. However, I would probably focus on resplendencies and destinies. Sidereals disguising themselves for powers that allow them to manipulate some area. Expanding the system (like embeds in demon). While Destinies give them grander abilities like weaving fate into some form that gives them access to powerful causality affecting powers. A system that would have checks and balances, requiring preparation and skill. Keeping colleges wouldn't be an issue because you'd want colleges and they'd expand your abilities. However the system itself would need time and effort.<br /> <br /> Also, Sidereals have been repeatedly encouraged to go into astrology. it's been considered the thing you do outside of native charms. You can't remove the system because charms just can't cover it. Lore can't dictate fate can only help you achieve your goal at a cost and even then it's not absolute or done in anyway that would indicate you could use it for long term planning. I don't know why you are so against turning a useless subsystem into a practical one. It's going to be in 3e, why not make it work?<br /> <br /> Edit- ALso greater astrology is bullshit and I shouldn't need to unlock something to make it finally useful. Astrology in and of itself should have a purpose and do it's job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T16:33:43-07:00","id":121289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=120211#post120211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As-is, it's impossible to buy all the Charms in the set without spending in excees of one-thousand xp.</div> </div> </div> </div> By my count, there are about 275 Sidereal Charms and Excellencies. Going by the long term XP expenditure guidelines in the 2E corebook there is not enough time for a Sidereal to learn all of them before they die of old age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2551-lucil","name":"Lucil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T17:37:11-07:00","id":121319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121289#post121289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> By my count, there are about 275 Sidereal Charms and Excellencies. Going by the long term XP expenditure guidelines in the 2E corebook there is not enough time for a Sidereal to learn all of them before they die of old age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kejak could looking at his write up so could the other Dreams elder if they got rid of all that useless astrology which used old rules. More to the point, no one wants to buy every single charm in every single ability and most excellencies are extremely unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T19:53:53-07:00","id":121396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121319#post121319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Kejak could looking at his write up so could the other Dreams elder if they got rid of all that useless astrology which used old rules. More to the point, no one wants to buy every single charm in every single ability and most excellencies are extremely unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div> A better question would be: how often does the closed Sidereal Charmset become an issue during actual games? In my experience, as both a player and as an ST, it doesn't. I have more trouble coming up with interesting DB characters, as both a player and as an ST, than I do when making Sidereal ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2551-lucil","name":"Lucil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T23:43:42-07:00","id":121531,"title":"","content":"In my experience, it does. I had something like 90 experience sitting fallow on my long-running greensid before that game fell apart, because I didn't want to push Martial Arts or Sorcery and I didn't want to start elbowing into the competencies of other PCs. And that was <i>after</i> I rebuilt him in play as a Thrown/Throne Shadow combatant instead of using Unweaving Method/Sidereal Shell Games as his primary combat trick, since the errata killed that interaction.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The fallacy here is that a Sidereal doesn't have to take every Charm <i>themselves</i> to start feeling cramped by the closed Charmset. They just have to take enough that their Circlemates have covered the rest of the Charmset; Sidereal Charms, historically, have rewarded redundancy even less than other Charmsets -- part of that whole &quot;narrow scope, powerful effect&quot; thing. (How many people are going to use Five Ordeals Odyssey on one journey, exactly? How many people do you need in a given situation with Shun the Smiling Lady? The answer is usually &quot;one&quot;, because anyone else using the Charm in that scene or situation isn't going to add anything.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":39,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","user":"ysadrel","date":". 04-29-2014, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T06:50:04-07:00","id":121677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121396#post121396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A better question would be: how often does the closed Sidereal Charmset become an issue during actual games? In my experience, as both a player and as an ST, it doesn't. I have more trouble coming up with interesting DB characters, as both a player and as an ST, than I do when making Sidereal ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can often unless you take MA. That's literally the only way to spend Xp once you cement what kind of character you are playing unless you do want to become a jack of all trades and if greater astrology isn't opened to you. This is why astrology should be better so you don't HAVE to be the martial artist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T08:09:05-07:00","id":121707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121677#post121677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's literally the only way to spend Xp once you cement what kind of character you are playing</div> </div> </div> </div>If the character is cemented, why do you even need to spend any more XP?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T08:11:22-07:00","id":121709,"title":"","content":"If a Solar runs out of things he wants to buy in his Charmset, he'll buy Evocations, sorcery, and Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> If a Lunar runs out of things she wants to buy in her Charmset, she'll buy sorcery, Evocations, and Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> More or less if anyone doesn't want to buy into their native Charmset anymore, they often buy into other stuff. The Sidereal &quot;fixed Tree&quot; thing is moot, as a note. Historically some Solar trees presented so much competence it didn't matter fi you could make new Charms, you had nothing of note to buy in them anyhow at a point. And most groups don't homebrew.<br /> <br /> That Sidereals <i>need</i> a super-special extra area to spend their xp is flawed by assuming this is a problem unique to Sidereal Exalted. They are given options other Exalts don't (what astrology they have, Martial Arts no one else gets). That you don't like the way they chose to branch this out doesn't necessitate it be the way you wish it were.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T08:38:54-07:00","id":121722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121709#post121709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Solar runs out of things he wants to buy in his Charmset, he'll buy Evocations, sorcery, and Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> If a Lunar runs out of things she wants to buy in her Charmset, she'll buy sorcery, Evocations, and Martial Arts.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The difference being Solars and Lunars can't run out barring the St and players imagination. Sidereals on the other hand have a limited charmset and an Already EXISTING subsystem that doesn't work well at all. Not to mention that sidereals are the worst when it comes to buying evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-29-2014, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T08:43:49-07:00","id":121727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121707#post121707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the character is cemented, why do you even need to spend any more XP?</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean is that you've already spent all you wanted on the charms you can acquire. For Martial artists and sorcerers it's theoretically limitless. For non-Martial artists and sorcerers this means you hit your cap a lot faster than you'd want to. There should be something that helps you in an area of expertise without breaking the charmset while being different than the other ways. My idea is to just fix astrology so you want to spend experience on it. Keeping it a faulting system isn't doing it justice and neither does removing it because the sidereal charmset can't replicate what it's supposed to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T08:45:22-07:00","id":121730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121707#post121707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the character is cemented, why do you even need to spend any more XP?</div> </div> </div> </div>Becuse it's given to everyone and you have to spend it somewhere?<br /> <br /> Though generally, Sidereal Charms rarely have much to do with the concept itself. Unlike Solar or Lunar charms, that feel like extensions of one's self, they feel more like external tools you get than anything. This helps a bit with making the whole &quot;well, my concept was a diplomat but I ran out of social options, I guess I'll take up basketweaving&quot; thing less aggravating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T08:49:47-07:00","id":121735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121677#post121677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can often unless you take MA. That's literally the only way to spend Xp once you cement what kind of character you are playing unless you do want to become a jack of all trades and if greater astrology isn't opened to you. This is why astrology should be better so you don't HAVE to be the martial artist.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, this really only becomes a problem at either high Essence or high exp total, or both, which isn't that usual in my experience.<br /> <br /> Second, Sorcery still exists, and is actually kickass for plugging holes in the Sids' Charmset and growing your character in every way other than pure killing power.<br /> <br /> Third, Sids have probably the best Charmset for dipping outside of your core expertise, and doing so will not necessarily shift your character concept to &quot;jack of all trades&quot;.<br /> <br /> Your average starting Sid character won't be fucked by not investing in MA, neither will your E4 500 exp character unless you want to be the best combat build a Sid can be (though even at this level you can get a lot of mileage out of Archery+Melee synergies). Higher than that, the game breaks down anyway, so not having enough things to buy is the least of your problems.<br /> <br /> Nothing of that is guaranteed to apply in any way, shape or form to 3e, so stay cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T08:57:21-07:00","id":121739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121722#post121722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference being Solars and Lunars can't run out barring the St and players imagination. Sidereals on the other hand have a limited charmset and an Already EXISTING subsystem that doesn't work well at all. Not to mention that sidereals are the worst when it comes to buying evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>See what I have said through this thread a lot. Most games don't use Homebrew and so the fixed Charmset point is moot. A Sidereal who bought all five Linguistics Charms is more or less int he same boat as a lot of Solars who bought all six or so Dodge Charms barring new printed Charms. Homebrew beyond that point is houserules on either sort of Exalt.<br /> <br /> I also will note that while not good, astrology is not non-functional. I feel statements that it is to be a tad hyperbolic.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T08:59:09-07:00","id":121741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121735#post121735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, this really only becomes a problem at either high Essence or high exp total, or both, which isn't that usual in my experience.<br /> <br /> Second, Sorcery still exists, and is actually kickass for plugging holes in the Sids' Charmset and growing your character in every way other than pure killing power.<br /> <br /> Third, Sids have probably the best Charmset for dipping outside of your core expertise, and doing so will not necessarily shift your character concept to &quot;jack of all trades&quot;.<br /> <br /> Your average starting Sid character won't be fucked by not investing in MA, neither will your E4 500 exp character unless you want to be the best combat build a Sid can be (though even at this level you can get a lot of mileage out of Archery+Melee synergies). Higher than that, the game breaks down anyway, so not having enough things to buy is the least of your problems.<br /> <br /> Nothing of that is guaranteed to apply in any way, shape or form to 3e, so stay cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what you want and how far or thin you want to spread yourself. I don't see why everyone seems to be against astrology working as a system that's equally as strong as martial arts. Granted, I'd need to see 3e to propose a more valid system to make it do what it should have always done but considering it's been a system for two editions, we've gotten so much fluff with it's kind of annoying that I seem to be the only one who wants it to work properly without requiring greater astrology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:00:48-07:00","id":121747,"title":"","content":"I would actually agree that the basic concept of Astrology (subtle imperatives or conditions to gain benefits by living out narratives) could use a more varied set of effects for playing them out. I don't dislike the blessings and curses, but I think they're a bit limited.<br /> <br /> I also feel like Colleges could use with a bit more to actually do; again, I don't dislike the basic concept of them being the source for the details of what narratives you set into motion, or that you can use creativity/pedantic wordplay to stretch all kinds of things under them, just maybe a bit of a stronger sense of different Colleges being able to do different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:03:38-07:00","id":121752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121739#post121739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also will note that while not good, astrology is not non-functional. I feel statements that it is to be a tad hyperbolic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Astrology's only two functions are a rather shitty disguise system compared to charms and Dice. It's functional but like everything in the sidereals book it's barely functional and easily capable of breaking the game if you know how to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:07:19-07:00","id":121753,"title":"","content":"Do most games really not use homebrew? Every game I've been in or heard about secondhand through both editions has, and as far as I was aware it's supposed to be part of character growth for most Exalt types. 3E is even coming out with a whole splat to make building custom Charms and Charmsets easier.<br /> <br /> (I've never understood why people assume nobody plays long campaigns, either, though, so maybe my experience is just skewed. It's still an experience a non-zero and -- I think -- non-trivial number of people are having, though!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:11:40-07:00","id":121758,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm wrong but you know, Resplendencies are a thing. They did stuff besides being dice or disguises. So maybe I'm still at a loss of what you mean where it only did two things besides, again, somewhat hyperbole on the nature of the mechanics. And to push things harder, if every mechanic in the Sidereals book (1e or 2e, whatever) was useless or broken, wouldn't then a place to fix is the mechanics set as a whole? And in so doing, maybe roll some of what you think should be offloaded into Super Special Subsystem Astrology-as-sorcery-but-not be done by just making those effects part of the native Charms, much as how Lunar shapeshifting and Dragon-Blooded elemental effects are?<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:17:23-07:00","id":121766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121758#post121758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm wrong but you know, Resplendencies are a thing. They did stuff besides being dice or disguises. So maybe I'm still at a loss of what you mean where it only did two things besides, again, somewhat hyperbole on the nature of the mechanics. And to push things harder, if every mechanic in the Sidereals book (1e or 2e, whatever) was useless or broken, wouldn't then a place to fix is the mechanics set as a whole? And in so doing, maybe roll some of what you think should be offloaded into Super Special Subsystem Astrology-as-sorcery-but-not be done by just making those effects part of the native Charms, much as how Lunar shapeshifting and Dragon-Blooded elemental effects are?<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resplendencies were minor neat tricks but you only needed 1 dot to get full access of them. You can't put an entire system into a limited charmset without making that system the charmset and pushing out what used to be in there. Lunars and Dragon-blooded have the luxury of having an unlimited charmset which tend to get expanded on in future books. They'll certainly never get a section that says sorry they don't get more charms. Removing Astrology doesn't fix anything. It just makes a power sidereals were supposed to have into even more meaningless words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:23:36-07:00","id":121773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121741#post121741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on what you want and how far or thin you want to spread yourself. I don't see why everyone seems to be against astrology working as a system that's equally as strong as martial arts. Granted, I'd need to see 3e to propose a more valid system to make it do what it should have always done but considering it's been a system for two editions, we've gotten so much fluff with it's kind of annoying that I seem to be the only one who wants it to work properly without requiring greater astrology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most importantly, because the only problem I have with Sids and MA is that it's one mandatory choice from their limited amount of Favored Ability picks, a problem I presume will disappear in 3e due to having Styles keyed off different Abilities. I like Kung Fu agents of Heaven more than I like fatebending agents of Heaven.<br /> <br /> Also, I never really liked Greater Astrology. Specific effects, sure, they were cool, but as a &quot;system&quot; it felt extremely tacked on, like it couldn't decide if it's an extension of their Charmset or some weird Sorcery equivalent. I don't want Astrology as Sorcery equivalent, and I don't want it as a hotpatch over the stupid idea of closed Charmset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:29:42-07:00","id":121779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121773#post121773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most importantly, because the only problem I have with Sids and MA is that it's one mandatory choice from their limited amount of Favored Ability picks, a problem I presume will disappear in 3e due to having Styles keyed off different Abilities. I like Kung Fu agents of Heaven more than I like fatebending agents of Heaven.<br /> <br /> Also, I never really liked Greater Astrology. Specific effects, sure, they were cool, but as a &quot;system&quot; it felt extremely tacked on, like it couldn't decide if it's an extension of their Charmset or some weird Sorcery equivalent. I don't want Astrology as Sorcery equivalent, and I don't want it as a hotpatch over the stupid idea of closed Charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want it to be a hot patch. I just want a system that'll let me be an astrologer like the game has constantly been telling me is a valid and productive thing to be. I don't like Greater Astrology either and I don't want it to be a set of charms. I just want it to be a system that expands on that role. I was just spitballing ideas because I'd need to know how sidereals work before coming up with something. I just want the xp that go into colleges to mean something and to expand my abilities in some way. I wouldn't mind on an expanded resplendency system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:40:45-07:00","id":121787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121766#post121766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just makes a power sidereals were supposed to have into even more meaningless words.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121779#post121779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want a system that'll let me be an astrologer like the game has constantly been telling me is a valid and productive thing to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where <i>have</i> you gotten that impression?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:43:09-07:00","id":121792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121766#post121766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Resplendencies were minor neat tricks but you only needed 1 dot to get full access of them. You can't put an entire system into a limited charmset without making that system the charmset and pushing out what used to be in there. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to be a plan for Lunars at least. I'm nto saying delete astrology. I just have yet to be told how &quot;expanding it&quot; (besides maybe making it do what it is set to do better) can't be acomplished by giving more fatebending effects in the native Charmset instead of having weird pseudo-Charms and pseudo-spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121766#post121766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Lunars and Dragon-blooded have the luxury of having an unlimited charmset which tend to get expanded on in future books. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know to what amount or how many new Charms are in the future. You have epistemic ability to support this statement. Lunar Exalted in 1e, as an example, never got a new Charm published out of the corebook all of 1e. If I remember correctly, neither did Abyssals (who were popular in 1e). Outside of Castebooks (which we aren't getting in 3e so far) there were maybe three Solar Charms until Cult of the Illuminated and nothing for Dragon-Blooded out of the Aspect Books. <br /> <br /> &quot;Infinite expandability&quot; is a tempest in a teapot. It's a moot point as in the end it depends on expansion rates (whcih we know nothing of) and what amounts to houserules (whcih can break the &quot;no custom Charms&quot; anyhow).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121766#post121766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... They'll certainly never get a section that says sorry they don't get more charms. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Which matters really not at all since in the end the &quot;Fixed Charms&quot; thing is a bit of fluff as far as I'm concerned. It's not like its software that is inviolable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121766#post121766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Removing Astrology doesn't fix anything. It just makes a power sidereals were supposed to have into even more meaningless words.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize that expanding astrology so far has been by your proposals the same issue for Knacks in it being not-Charms/spells to do Charm/spells stuff. I also didn't say remove astrology. Just that what you want it to do extra can be acheived by a more expansive Charmset.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:47:10-07:00","id":121796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121773#post121773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most importantly, because the only problem I have with Sids and MA is that it's one mandatory choice from their limited amount of Favored Ability picks, a problem I presume will disappear in 3e due to having Styles keyed off different Abilities. I like Kung Fu agents of Heaven more than I like fatebending agents of Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. With the MA Ability no longer the One True Path to Power, and MA only being that historically for fighting.<br /> <br /> I also kind of am confused what fatebending is even supposed to mean beyond the weird symobilc shit Sidreals do already, as &quot;fate&quot; is a braod term that Exalted has explicated in a specific way (causality). Which to some extent is what all Exalts do. If it is through precognition, conicidence magic, and luck....they already do that. Martial arts just happens to also add to their stated roles as monetors, advisors, and sifus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121773#post121773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I never really liked Greater Astrology. Specific effects, sure, they were cool, but as a &quot;system&quot; it felt extremely tacked on, like it couldn't decide if it's an extension of their Charmset or some weird Sorcery equivalent. I don't want Astrology as Sorcery equivalent, and I don't want it as a hotpatch over the stupid idea of closed Charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less agreed. The closed Charmset is not even itself so bad I feel since it's a moot point (see above, not a lot of new Charms are published for Exalted anyhow save specialty books, of which Dreams is considered a failure of). I still feel a lot of its effects could of just as well be normal Charms with weird how-to-get preresquisties. <br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:51:39-07:00","id":121799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121752#post121752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Astrology's only two functions are a rather shitty disguise system compared to charms and Dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it also rejuvenates Virtues and Willpower, and there's a bit more to target numbers and difficulties than &quot;dice&quot;...<br /> <br /> But the thing that really makes for the function of Astrology are the conditions under which the effects kick in, because there's an assumption that either people will be conditioned towards circumstances where they get blessings and away from ones where they get curses, or else will just live out a life where certain circumstances are more or less effective for them*, and that this will hang subtle but pervasive effects in the long term.<br /> <br /> And when you get beings who can carry multiple destinies**, you can specify them to complex situations that allow multiple blessings or curses to kick in at once, creating a particular significant alteration.... I think, I can't entirely recall if astrology says that its blessings alone can stack target number reductions and the like.<br /> <br /> * I mean, if I give a guy an ascending destiny in which his poorly considered business deals are cursed to fail at the initial negotiation or investment stage, it doesn't really matter if he's conditioned against making such deals, since they stop happening properly to afflict his life anyway.<br /> ** Although I'd kind of like that possibility to be based on something other than Essence dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:52:56-07:00","id":121801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121779#post121779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't want it to be a hot patch. I just want a system that'll let me be an astrologer like the game has constantly been telling me is a valid and productive thing to be. I don't like Greater Astrology either and I don't want it to be a set of charms. I just want it to be a system that expands on that role. I was just spitballing ideas because I'd need to know how sidereals work before coming up with something. I just want the xp that go into colleges to mean something and to expand my abilities in some way. I wouldn't mind on an expanded resplendency system.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's something I think we need less of is colleges. They exist as a trait for the sake of being a trait and I think are greatly impacting how important you think astrology should be in that regards.<br /> <br /> I also think that the Charmset as is does weird fatebending stuff fairly well. Lore, Performance, Bureaucracy, War, Awareness, Linguistics, Ride, and Sail (in both editions) have piles of interesting exotic effects to let you tell the future, bind people together, declare omens, penalize actions you don't like, buff ones you do, and make weird coincidence shappen like forming a band of musicicians, knowing a room is full with deathtraps, or finding the ship that gets you to where you need to go at a moment's notice. You also get Charms that bind spirits, ask for help by builidng magical Christmas trees, and creating gods.<br /> <br /> Greater Astrology was fairly grab-bag list of stuff that more or less added other avenues to Sidereal magic we had: coincidences, precognition, declarations of events, and spirit magic. These are the things a fatebender apparently does in Creation. These are things acheivable with their native Charms. Rather than tack on a subsystem to support their core role, their core Charms are there to do that. A think that it needs a special subsystem beyond the generic astrological stuff is more or less trying to add systems for system's sake instead of making Charms, the basis of a splat's core themes to start with, do that.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T10:12:20-07:00","id":121817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121801#post121801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that the Charmset as is does weird fatebending stuff fairly well. Lore, Performance, Bureaucracy, War, Awareness, Linguistics, Ride, and Sail (in both editions) have piles of interesting exotic effects to let you tell the future, bind people together, declare omens, penalize actions you don't like, buff ones you do, and make weird coincidence shappen like forming a band of musicicians, knowing a room is full with deathtraps, or finding the ship that gets you to where you need to go at a moment's notice. You also get Charms that bind spirits, ask for help by builidng magical Christmas trees, and creating gods.And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we can already do the mysterious fate-bender stuff with native Sidereal charm then we do we have left for Astronomy ? 'cause TN/Dices manipulation sound utterly boring imo.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T10:26:37-07:00","id":121827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121531#post121531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience, it does. I had something like 90 experience sitting fallow on my long-running greensid before that game fell apart, because I didn't want to push Martial Arts or Sorcery and I didn't want to start elbowing into the competencies of other PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that might be a problem with the charmset, I don't think it's a problem with the charmset being locked.<br /> If you are someone who can write 10 custom charms without inviting serious balance issues then more power to you, but that's not a typical state of affairs in my experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T10:27:50-07:00","id":121829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121817#post121817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we can already do the mysterious fate-bender stuff with native Sidereal charm then we do we have left for Astronomy ? 'cause TN/Dices manipulation sound utterly boring imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpcik, astronomy =/= astrology. And hasn't for a while. It's important to note just because of random real-world stuff invovling them.<br /> <br /> As for why have it, I honestly am not sure it's needed. A lot of native Charms probably could do the astrology stuff in less baroque a way. I'm just at least granting Epi here in case it were to stay what would be needed to make it work. But if the native Charm set did enough of astrology's current stuff that matters, I am actually kind of skeptical it needs to be as crunchy as it currently is.<br /> <br /> Another is aesthetic desire. Astrology represents not so much something Sidereals do magically (save the Greater stuff) but a process of manipulating the Loom that in theory anyone can do but in reality only Sidereals are qualified to do, and divorced from theirm Charmset as far as its &quot;source&quot;. It is external to them, while their fatebending in other aspects is internal. Mind this is a bit of ad hoc reasoning. I honestly have always though astrology could be rolled into general Sidereal stuff with less xp bloat and fiddeliness just fine and have in the past houseruled it to be so in my games.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T10:31:13-07:00","id":121831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121801#post121801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's something I think we need less of is colleges. They exist as a trait for the sake of being a trait and I think are greatly impacting how important you think astrology should be in that regards.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's been floated that they might be rolled up as Merits?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T10:37:37-07:00","id":121837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121831#post121831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's been floated that they might be rolled up as Merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be okay with that. Since Merits weren't as system-supported in 2e, I had a special Knack-like Charm for each Ability that more or less let you use your actual Ability rating for the College for all purposes. Since besides actually rolling astroogy and prerequisites, they didn't do anything else anyhow.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T10:58:16-07:00","id":121855,"title":"","content":"Something that the comic gave me hope for.<br /> I'd love it if Rakan Thulio's Curse of Blades was a sign of things to come for the dedicated Sidereal Astrologer rather than -1 TN and you've actually got to touch them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T12:20:28-07:00","id":121893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121855#post121855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that the comic gave me hope for.<br /> I'd love it if Rakan Thulio's Curse of Blades was a sign of things to come for the dedicated Sidereal Astrologer rather than -1 TN and you've actually got to touch them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read the comic yet (Because I'm extremely lazy and a bit busy) what does it do?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T12:24:04-07:00","id":121896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121829#post121829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nitpcik, astronomy =/= astrology. And hasn't for a while. It's important to note just because of random real-world stuff invovling them.<br /> <br /> As for why have it, I honestly am not sure it's needed. A lot of native Charms probably could do the astrology stuff in less baroque a way. I'm just at least granting Epi here in case it were to stay what would be needed to make it work. But if the native Charm set did enough of astrology's current stuff that matters, I am actually kind of skeptical it needs to be as crunchy as it currently is.<br /> <br /> Another is aesthetic desire. Astrology represents not so much something Sidereals do magically (save the Greater stuff) but a process of manipulating the Loom that in theory anyone can do but in reality only Sidereals are qualified to do, and divorced from theirm Charmset as far as its &quot;source&quot;. It is external to them, while their fatebending in other aspects is internal. Mind this is a bit of ad hoc reasoning. I honestly have always though astrology could be rolled into general Sidereal stuff with less xp bloat and fiddeliness just fine and have in the past houseruled it to be so in my games.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with native charms is the limit you have to put on charms. I'm not saying they have to Spells or Charms I'm just saying astrology should do something. Personally, it would be nice if you could use Fate and causality to your advantage weaving a fate or destiny that isn't just a bonus but actually accomplishes something. The ability to weave the fate of a nation and the way Sidereal astrology work don't line up and it would be nice if it did. If astrology also helped you in combat and other areas. I would like it to work in a more long term area of effect. Planned and set rather than a charm which is spontaneous and instant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T13:07:49-07:00","id":121929,"title":"","content":"I feel like Resplendencies would actually be a decent starting point. You buy the one College and get a number of effects, all of which provide specific bonuses in specific circumstances, helping you conform to your college's archetype. -1 TN is a pretty dull effect; &quot;You are guaranteed to find a demanding job that provides just barely enough to live on, and nobody will be able to track you if you work your hardest at it&quot; is more interesting. It's also way more situational: As a Charm, it would just be too narrow to work (even for a Sidereal Charm), but as an Astrology, it's just one of a number of thematically-related abilities that you buy in a single package.<br /> <br /> Now, toss on the ability to attach Resplendent powers to other people (though not other Sidereals), requiring you to specify what conditions will activate the abilities (since non-Sidereals can't consciously activate their destinies). That gives you the ability to play Sidereals as advisers: They can craft up an appropriate destiny and then give the appropriate advice (&quot;I recommend taking a menial job to blend in. Trust me, just keep your head down and be a good little worker, and nobody will look at you twice&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T13:31:10-07:00","id":121947,"title":"","content":"We always end up talking about the closed Charmset a lot in these threads. It does seem arguable that beyond the soft limits of &quot;homebrew is hard&quot; and &quot;People playing Sidereals generally want their characters to come up with Sidereal Charms, which includes not being exactly what they want&quot;, the hard limit closure of the Charmset doesn't really add much. As much as it does add to their cool as a mechanical statement of them working under limits and their cool of using MA as an cunning solution to their &quot;problem&quot;, is it worth it? (Open question). I actually don't get the impression actual Sidereal players have a strong consensus on how much it matters.<br /> <br /> With Astrology and the desire to have it be an open system, I'm more interested in whether the designers can actually knock it up as a balanced open system that's fun and inspiring to use, more than a desire to have curses and blessings not look like Charms or spells in their rules format. <br /> <br /> Like, the Curse of Blades (I can't remember if that term was actually in the comic or not, but it's cool either way) is like a social influence towards a prophecy declared to be that lives in the structure of Fate. It is not exactly like the existing base Sidereal Astrology that makes shifts the structure of the work to make auspicious and inauspicious events more and less likely, which is a fine effect. If coming up with effects like that works better in a Charm or spell format that trying to write a general system of mechanics, then they should be written that way. Mechanics follow function, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T13:57:21-07:00","id":121965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121893#post121893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the comic yet (Because I'm extremely lazy and a bit busy) what does it do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically he does this ritual that calls out to all swordsman that the reincarnated soul of The Sword Saint, first to unlock the secrets of the Daiklave, is now in the body of this young man and divines the location for them. The legend of the Sword Saint declares the one who defeats the Sword Saint in combat will gain the Saints power. This leads the man to be assaulted by many swordsman and seekers of power along his journey.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T15:03:19-07:00","id":122013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121965#post121965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically he does this ritual that calls out to all swordsman that the reincarnated soul of The Sword Saint, first to unlock the secrets of the Daiklave, is now in the body of this young man and divines the location for them. The legend of the Sword Saint declares the one who defeats the Sword Saint in combat will gain the Saints power. This leads the man to be assaulted by many swordsman and seekers of power along his journey.</div> </div> </div> </div>The impression I got was that he actually performed the ritual all the way back in the Usurpation, shortly after Nova's death. Basically, it caused all of Nova's reincarnations throughout the ages to be plagued by power-hungry swordsmen (though Visiting Flare is the only such reincarnation since Nova went straight into the Jade Prison).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T16:05:24-07:00","id":122061,"title":"","content":"The problem I had with the closed charmset was that some of the charms were just boring and passive. There's one sail charm where the sidereal activates it and it makes a boat come along...eventually. If charms are a function of the character's prowess in an ability, then the charm should be an expression of that prowess. In other words, activating a charm should have better effects than &quot;You sit there until a boat shows up.&quot;<br /> <br /> If Astrology remains a separate thing from the charmset, I wouldn't mind more passive effects being astrological effects and more active ones being charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T05:00:20-07:00","id":124414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change?p=121929#post121929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, toss on the ability to attach Resplendent powers to other people (though not other Sidereals), requiring you to specify what conditions will activate the abilities (since non-Sidereals can't consciously activate their destinies). That gives you the ability to play Sidereals as advisers: They can craft up an appropriate destiny and then give the appropriate advice (&quot;I recommend taking a menial job to blend in. Trust me, just keep your head down and be a good little worker, and nobody will look at you twice&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted, because Liking isn't enough sometimes...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtharthio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The impression I got was that he actually performed the ritual all the way back in the Usurpation, shortly after Nova's death. Basically, it caused all of Nova's reincarnations throughout the ages to be plagued by power-hungry swordsmen (though Visiting Flare is the only such reincarnation since Nova went straight into the Jade Prison).</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the same impression, but on rereading, found that it isn't so clear; given that his astro-mumbo-jumbo specifically gave all those interested *a vision* of the current holder of EN's essence, it had to be after the Jade Prison cracked. After all, the Sids thought the imprisonment was forever, so why go to the trouble of basically slapping the &quot;Number One Headband&quot; on someone who wouldn't be around for centuries, if ever?<br /> <br /> Collages as Merits? Problem is, if so many things become Merits, chargen is gonna feel shortchanged, unless we get an unprecedented amount of Merit points. WoD Merits already feel crowded to me, I don't want to see Merit Bloat become a thing...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T05:18:47-07:00","id":124418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120079-sidereals-and-focus-change#post120079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm reading the original games of divinity and this is a passage I've read in several places.<br /> <br /> &quot;They made the sidereals, who were wise and mighty seers and weaver of spells but few in number and weaker in battle than the solar and lunar exalted&quot;<br /> <br /> So my question is when did weaver of spells change to martial artists? I mean the implication is that they were more traditional sorcerers compared to other exalts but none the less they were less about fighting and more about mystical might. When did that change and why use Martial arts instead of sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Esp as the design intent is still clearly that Sids are weaker in direct combat than other Celestials (and probably well-built Terrestrials!)...<br /> <br /> Well, you know that I already agree with this, from that prior Sid thread. Look, we can argue current mechanics on the forum all day, and it's clear that rejiggering 2E Sids to favor Sorcery over MA would be problematic. But I still maintain that this could be made to work starting fresh from scratch in 3E! The big problem wouldn't be reconceptualizing the narrative/mechanical themes and frames of Sidereals, it would be getting the fandom to accept these changes, which is probably too great a hurdle to even attempt. Which is why I said before that this is almost certainly never going to happen, even if it should, but it's still fun to ask &quot;what if&quot;?<br /> <br /> I know people love the concept of SMA, but frankly, I don't see why that needs to stay around. Sidereals have the &quot;old kung fu master&quot; as part of their narrative, but it's hardly exclusive to them. There are probably more DB &quot;old masters&quot; out there, Immaculate and otherwise, than there are Sidereals as a whole! And Lunars can fill that role easily, as well. It's pointless to build an entire splat around that theme. Esp as the Seers do have other things going on, narratively...<br /> <br /> Here's an idea: &quot;Secret Styles&quot; instead of &quot;Sidereal&quot;. These were created by the Solars, with Sidereal guidance, in the First Age. When the Solars died, their knowledge would have died with them, but for several martially-oriented Seers, who kept their secret arts alive (think of the Arabian scholars who kept the learning of the Classical world extant through the European Dark Ages until the Renaissance). Now that the Solars are back, the masters of one faction seek to return the lost arts to those Solars who are worthy...while the other faction finds it poetic to kill them with their own mastery. <br /> <br /> Of course, this may bring up cries of &quot;Solars aren't weird enough to come up with SMA!&quot;, but that's all an issue of flavor text. If the current writers really wanted to spin it that way, they could do so in a way that we could accept (with lots of grumbling, of course). The mechanics follow the narrative, not the other way around...<br /> <br /> \u200bBesides, it's not as though mystic sorcerers *can't* be the hidden master that one must seek out! That's pretty much Dr. Strange's origin in a nutshell! Make Sidereal Sorcery something that only Solars can also master, with extr difficulty, and there you go...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}